@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # Reference clients
 
+**Support posture:** these files are maintained reference examples for API version 1.x. They are not published npm or PyPI packages, do not promise independent semantic versioning, and should be vendored or copied deliberately. Breaking API changes require an updated example and compatibility note in the project release record.
+
 These small, zero-dependency clients demonstrate the public HTTP contract. They are MIT-licensed examples, not required SDKs.
 
 ## JavaScript
@@ -27,3 +29,7 @@ pack = client.pack("revenue-contract-review")
 The Python client uses only the standard library. Copy the single module into a governed project or vendor it with the source release.
 
 Keep retrieved record IDs, release versions, review dates, source IDs, and rights fields in the consuming agent’s run record. A successful retrieval does not establish source applicability or action authority.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+The examples target the public read-only API and Node.js 22 or Python 3.11+. They intentionally omit retries, durable caches, telemetry, and framework-specific authentication. Consumers own those production concerns and must preserve the retrieved release, record, source, review, and rights metadata.
